{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes","id":42505,"title":"Thought Exercise: Lunar Totems subsume and replace Lunar Castes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-04T15:08:12-08:00","id":42505,"title":"Thought Exercise: Lunar Totems subsume and replace Lunar Castes","content":"One wolf totem is not the same as another, and an individual totem is fully capable of including the concept of &quot;warrior, trickster, or shaman&quot; by itself, without a Caste.. There was Ma-Ha-Suchi's exceptionally social Wolf Among The Roses, in contrast to the obvious concept of Fenris Wolf That Devours The World, or the wiseman-appropriate Wolf That Watches At The Border of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Each is a wolf, but the player chooses what that means for the character. One mythic archetype of the wolf is fleshed out with completely different Favored (or &quot;Totemic&quot;) Attributes than another. Ma-Ha-Suchi is a charming, social wolf, whereas Fenris is a brutishly physical beast.<br /> <br /> <br /> The last word on the matter was that a Lunar's Totem would include various keywords that would associate with particular Lunar Charms, allowing you to purchase them at favored costs without simply giving Lunar Exalted more favored Attributes. Taking that a step further, the Totem itself could be made the source of &quot;Totem Attributes&quot; (as Sidereals Castes are the source of &quot;Auspicious Abilities&quot;).<br /> <br /> <br /> Castelessness as a concept would be lost, but we would still have Chimerae for the option of breaking out of the &quot;Caste analogue&quot; of the Totem.<br /> <br /> In what ways do you imagine that Chimerism and Castelessness would be sufficiently different from each other that Lunars are enriched by the option of being one or the other without being both at the same time?<br /> <br /> <br /> Caste-specific anima powers would be lost, though all Lunars would retain the universal non-Charm power of their Spirit Shape (and derived as it is from the &quot;Caste analogue&quot; Totem, it pretty much would be a Caste-specific power) and Heart's Blood shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you mention anything else that would or would not be lost by this merger?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 01-04-2014, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T15:30:19-08:00","id":42511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes#post42505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One wolf totem is not the same as another, and an individual totem is fully capable of including the concept of &quot;warrior, trickster, or shaman&quot; by itself, without a Caste.. There was Ma-Ha-Suchi's exceptionally social Wolf Among The Roses, in contrast to the obvious concept of Fenris Wolf That Devours The World, or the wiseman-appropriate Wolf That Watches At The Border of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you just showed how totem could be bent through Caste. Why bother making spirit shapes a splat if they can be so easily bent according to Caste lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:30:48-08:00","id":42547,"title":"","content":"Also, behold the power of the Platypus-Totem!<br /> Gives you all the keywords!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T16:47:29-08:00","id":42559,"title":"","content":"This is a thought exercise, not another project. I think the idea is more of a 'what if' than a &quot;Let's rewrite Lunars Wholesale!&quot;. It is hard to tell the difference and this is an assumption, but I choose to take the post in the Exalted forums in the lest offending light possible. Makes life so much easier that way.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, 'Wolf who Dances in Moonlight'* could be a Changing Moon, No Moon or even a Full Moon based on the Caste system. In this hypothetical 'totem system' it would be easier to construct the character according to my original conception.<br /> <br /> In answer to the OP's question; i's complicated. Castelessness and Chimerism are already linked in cannon. I'm not exactly a fan of the Casteless either, though they make great story fodder when I run games. In that way, I see the loss of 'save the Casteless form becoming a Chmera' stories. But that is only 1 kind of story and I imagine I'd still be able to run it on a smaller scale.<br /> <br /> *<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Imagine an individual of poise and grace, dancing in the night, luring away the unsuspecting and offering her performance as tribute to the gods. Fluid, seamless enchanting movement is her tool to seduce the mortal and praise the divine alike. Every night she can dance for hours on end if it is required, continuing into the day until night returns as is her way.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  posted before finshing...sutpid touch screen 01-04-2014, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:02:03-08:00","id":42565,"title":"","content":"So, the Wolf Totem would give something like Dexterity, Manipulation and Perception as &quot;Caste Attributes?&quot;<br /> <br /> You'd probably end up with de facto Castes anyway, but it might work. I'm not sure how it would interact with Chimera and Casteless though.<br /> <br /> It might be more interesting if the Totem keyword worked a bit like the Elemental Keyword, instead of giving an experience discount. Like, I Bite Things Hard Prana gives a bonus to damage, but if you have a Wolf Totem, you can use the Wolf keyword to give the victim rabies at the same time, or if you have the Shark totem, some of your teeth get stuck in the wound and make it harder to heal.<br /> <br /> Chimera might have the ability to pick which Totem they want to use when they learn a new charm, so they could apply the Shark keyword to I Bite Things Hard Prana, but the Wolf keyword to I Howl Really Loud Stance.<br /> <br /> Not sure what would happen to the Casteless though. I guess they would lose the Totem keyword, but gain something in exchange. Not sure what.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:17:04-08:00","id":42570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42565#post42565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Wolf Totem would give something like Dexterity, Manipulation and Perception as &quot;Caste Attributes?&quot;<br /> <br /> You'd probably end up with de facto Castes anyway, but it might work. I'm not sure how it would interact with Chimera and Casteless though.<br /> <br /> It might be more interesting if the Totem keyword worked a bit like the Elemental Keyword, instead of giving an experience discount. Like, I Bite Things Hard Prana gives a bonus to damage, but if you have a Wolf Totem, you can use the Wolf keyword to give the victim rabies at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be more the Coyote Keyword.'s forte","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:32:59-08:00","id":42591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42565#post42565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Wolf Totem would give something like Dexterity, Manipulation and Perception as &quot;Caste Attributes?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> You would choose the Attributes that describe the kind of mythic Wolf you want to be. Ma-Ha-Suchi's &quot;Wolf Among The Roses&quot; may have all three social Attributes and whichever fourth his player wants to complete the concept he's going for, but the player who chooses &quot;All-Devouring Fenris Wolf&quot; would choose completely different Attributes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wolf&quot; would be meaningless to your Attributes, except for whatever meaning you ascribe to it. That's why it's a Totem, not a Caste.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:47:48-08:00","id":42603,"title":"","content":"Ma-Ha-Suchi works much better as a goat, though, and that's where your thesis falls apart.<br /> <br /> Listen: In 1e, Lunars could fuck themselves up by taking a second totem form; this was seen as the first step towards chimerism. Ma-Ha-Suchi was a wolf/goat totem Lunar; no explanation was given as to which one he'd had first and which one he got second, but goat was the more important one -- his beastmen are described as goatmen, not wolfmen. In 2e, they removed the &quot;two totem&quot; thing, so they had to choose between making him a wolf-totem Lunar with horns and hooves somehow or a goat-totem Lunar with a carnivore's mouth somehow. They went with &quot;Wolf with antlers.&quot; I am not sure why. I suspect it has something to do with the wolf being the sexier of the two animals, and wanting to keep one of the signature pieces of the setting's IP as sexy and interesting as possible? Like how they took the Slug out as the signature Wood Aspect and replaced him with Tepet Ejava? Goats are silly, wolves are badass, our signature badass Lunar warlord can be either a goat or a wolf, so let's make him a wolf so he'll be more badass, QED. (Also, fantasy artists are much more likely to know how to draw a badass wolf head than a badass goat head, so that makes art direction take less time because your artists aren't constantly having to learn how to draw a scowly or snarling or otherwise-emoting goat head.)<br /> <br /> But he is much, much more <i>interesting</i> as a goat-totem Lunar -- first, because having signature Lunars with totems that aren't obviously badass cool animals is more interesting than going with the obvious choices (&quot;Seriously, he's a <i>goat?&quot; </i>&quot;Yes, and he's going to burn this city down and his children will slaughter its ten thousand inhabitants unless we face him down.&quot;), and second because you want as few overlaps between official Lunar totems as possible, and so it's best to give the NPC Lunars weird totems so the players can choose whatever badass, obvious-choice animal they have their heart set on without feeling like they're being redundant.<br /> <br /> (Hell, goat even fits Ma-Ha-Suchi's First Age portrayal, as much as I loathe his First Age portrayal -- it would have been much more appropriate to base him on the randy goat archetype than a Meat Loaf song title pun.)<br /> <br /> The problem with this idea is that if Lunars use totem archetypes instead of castes, then you have two options for implementation.<br /> <br /> 1) Instead of using individual animals you use broad animal archetypes. If you're going to do this, trust me, you will end up reinventing the castes, but renamed.<br /> <br /> 2) You actually limit them to five or ten specific animals, like wolf, shark, snake, bird of prey, velociraptor, and five more obvious archetypal picks. This is going to be hugely limiting -- you don't want a setting with 300 lunars which are just variations on the same ten animals over and over again. It's even worse if you do like the other Exalt-types do and use five.<br /> <br /> (Alternately, if you don't want to limit them to five or ten animals, and you want totem to serve as caste while allowing every Lunar to have a unique totem, then what you're <i>actually</i> proposing has nothing to do with making totem serve as caste and is actually just a proposal for Lunars to not have castes at all.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 01-04-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T18:02:40-08:00","id":42610,"title":"","content":"Goat eyes are alien and terrifying, Ma-Ha-Suchi is alien and terrifying, the choice is obvious!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T18:23:04-08:00","id":42616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42603#post42603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, if you don't want to limit them to five or ten animals, and you want totem to serve as caste while allowing every Lunar to have a unique totem, then what you're <i>actually</i> proposing has nothing to do with making totem serve as caste and is actually just a proposal for Lunars to not have castes at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's closer to the case of this thought experiment, yes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do Lunars need Castes at all?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:06:24-08:00","id":42658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42603#post42603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, fantasy artists are much more likely to know how to draw a badass wolf head than a badass goat head, so that makes art direction take less time because your artists aren't constantly having to learn how to draw a scowly or snarling or otherwise-emoting goat head.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You guys need to hire more Furry subculture artists. Quite a few awesome artists out there who have a lot of practice with drawing anthropomorphic animals of various types and good skill at putting recognizable expressions and emotions on non-human faces.<br /> <br /> And that's actually not an easy thing to do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:14:22-08:00","id":42662,"title":"","content":"Dude. Goats are awesome. I want to play a goat Lunar.<br /> <br /> Well, Mountain Goat. And those aren't actually true goats... But female Mountain Goats will ruin your day and dominate local bighorn sheep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:21:06-08:00","id":42667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42658#post42658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You guys need to hire more Furry subculture artists. Quite a few awesome artists out there who have a lot of practice with drawing anthropomorphic animals of various types and good skill at putting recognizable expressions and emotions on non-human faces.<br /> <br /> And that's actually not an easy thing to do...</div> </div> </div> </div>That might not get across the same visual impact. Keeping in mind that beastman form, in keeping with Lunar roots in Werewolf, is supposed to be a monstrous synthesis of Lunar and totem, rather than a more pedestrian combination of the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:27:28-08:00","id":42670,"title":"","content":"Furry art tends to be highly neotenous in a way inappropriate for beastmen and Lunar war-forms, and well-practiced furry artists tend to be good at their own style first and foremost. It can be very difficult to coerce an artist used to drawing in that style to switch to something closer to, say, Ron Spencer-style beastman hybrids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 01-04-2014, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T21:14:26-08:00","id":42683,"title":"","content":"Castes aren't there because they're <i>needed</i>, really -- nothing really weird happens to any of the splats if you remove them, not even Sidereals. They're guiderails for character generation and ways to help differentiate and identify characters at the high-concept level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T21:19:01-08:00","id":42684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42603#post42603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma-Ha-Suchi works much better as a goat, though, and that's where your thesis falls apart. ... (Hell, goat even fits Ma-Ha-Suchi's First Age portrayal, as much as I loathe his First Age portrayal -- it would have been much more appropriate to base him on the randy goat archetype than a Meat Loaf song title pun.)</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression was that his First Age portrayal was that his wolf totem was symbolic of his nature as a sexual predator, in a similar fashion to the way vampires are symbolic of sexual predation as well, or, IIRC, the way the Big Bad Wolf was symbolic of child molesters in the original version of Little Red Riding Hood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T21:35:28-08:00","id":42688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42670#post42670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furry art tends to be highly neotenous in a way inappropriate for beastmen and Lunar war-forms, and well-practiced furry artists tend to be good at their own style first and foremost. It can be very difficult to coerce an artist used to drawing in that style to switch to something closer to, say, Ron Spencer-style beastman hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me, please have as much Ron Spencer as can be fit in the Lunars book. That's my main hope artwise for it. &lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T21:53:12-08:00","id":42694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42670#post42670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furry art tends to be highly neotenous in a way inappropriate for beastmen and Lunar war-forms,.</div> </div> </div> </div>This deserves its own discussion, I usually hate most of the anthropomorphs in the lunar books... it's very easy for most artists to offer very unimaginative results (usually resembling cavemen with animal heads).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T04:27:41-08:00","id":42808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42603#post42603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he is much, much more <i>interesting</i> as a goat-totem Lunar -- first, because having signature Lunars with totems that aren't obviously badass cool animals is more interesting than going with the obvious choices (&quot;Seriously, he's a <i>goat?&quot; </i>&quot;Yes, and he's going to burn this city down and his children will slaughter its ten thousand inhabitants unless we face him down.&quot;), and second because you want as few overlaps between official Lunar totems as possible, and so it's best to give the NPC Lunars weird totems so the players can choose whatever badass, obvious-choice animal they have their heart set on without feeling like they're being redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for embracing the fact he's basically a Warhammer villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T05:06:41-08:00","id":42817,"title":"","content":"I'm more than welcome to have more weird-totem instead of the usual bull/tiger/wolf/cat/owl, though a hedonist rapist that look like Pan's cousin is not exactly......original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T06:41:26-08:00","id":42843,"title":"","content":"I would probably just make Ma-Ha-Suchi a mink totem at this point and laugh maniacally at the forum reaction it generates.<br /> <br /> That aside, I read the OP yesterday during game time and was like &quot;that's terrible, but I don't have time to write a scathing rebuke.&quot;<br /> <br /> So I ended up sleeping on it and now I'm more confused than displeased. What could you possibly hope to gain from dissolving the Lunar castes?<br /> <br /> Is it really a big damn deal that your charming sex machine happens to be a Full Moon? (It is not.) Does it matter that your badass exorcist-monk monster hunter is actually a No Moon? (No.) What about the geeky crafter who makes moonsilver roses he secretly delivers to his love interest at night being a Changing Moon? (Still not actually a problem.)<br /> <br /> So do you have a problem with the mechanical limitations inherent to the current Caste paradigm? I think so. Which further perplexes me because you could have simply and more cogently presented your argument with &quot;Hey can we please have something that closely mirrors Peter Schaefer's original Lunar chargen be the official rules for Ex3 so there's a bit more flexibility in Lunar archetypes?&quot; Which, by the way, do want. 2 + 2 is pretty ideal, and nothing stops people who want all three from getting them.<br /> <br /> Trying to tie down mechanics to something as fungible as what your totem animal happens to be is, in a word, anserine. I don't even think totem spirits are something that need to make the transition to Ex3, bluntly. Does it significantly change your character concept if your hero's favored alternate form is no longer totemic to their being? It shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T06:47:42-08:00","id":42847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42843#post42843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to tie down mechanics to something as fungible as what your totem animal happens to be is, in a word, <b>anserine</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.disp