1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Anserine.png/200px-Anserine.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><span style=\"font-size:20px\">?</span></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":894,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","user":"Skeptic Tank","date":". 01-05-2014, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/894-skeptic-tank","name":"Skeptic Tank","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:00:05-08:00","id":42880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42683#post42683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castes aren't there because they're <i>needed</i>, really -- nothing really weird happens to any of the splats if you remove them, not even Sidereals. <b>They're guiderails for character generation and ways to help differentiate and identify characters at the high-concept level</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, and this is a function that Totems can take over.<br /> <br /> The Devil Tigers of Second Edition worked pretty much the same way. First they make a new Mythos for themselves, and afterwards a Caste based on that Mythos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:43:16-08:00","id":42900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42603#post42603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listen: In 1e, Lunars could fuck themselves up by taking a second totem form; this was seen as the first step towards chimerism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was this in the sense that they got a second spirit shape, or in that their spirit shape became a totem A/totem B hybrid? Because the former is something I've wanted to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:17:11-08:00","id":42924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42900#post42900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was this in the sense that they got a second spirit shape, or in that their spirit shape became a totem A/totem B hybrid? Because the former is something I've wanted to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>You switched to a new one, and some traces of the old remained, so the latter. Also, the gods of your original/prior totem got pissed at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T09:28:06-08:00","id":42934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42670#post42670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furry art tends to be highly neotenous in a way inappropriate for beastmen and Lunar war-forms, and well-practiced furry artists tend to be good at their own style first and foremost. It can be very difficult to coerce an artist used to drawing in that style to switch to something closer to, say, Ron Spencer-style beastman hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rob Spencers style is really good. On the subject of Goatmen art I'm reminded about Diablo which has fairly neat beastmen:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.videogamesartwork.com/sites/default/files/styles/image_node/public/images/image/1377179012/diablo3-monster-goatman.jpg?itok=ok0__vay\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.videogamesartwork.com/sit...?itok=ok0__vay</a><br /> <a href=\"http://2.bp.blogspot.com/-0NnJ94NPpks/T8f3lIRWC1I/AAAAAAAABOw/GOVFLm1Yu9g/s400/goatman_old.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://2.bp.blogspot.com/-0NnJ94NPpk...oatman_old.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42694#post42694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This deserves its own discussion, I usually hate most of the anthropomorphs in the lunar books... it's very easy for most artists to offer very unimaginative results (usually resembling cavemen with animal heads).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ex2 Lunar book was not very impressive art-wise atleast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","user":"Zironic","date":". 01-05-2014, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T17:08:43-08:00","id":43232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42880#post42880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly, and this is a function that Totems can take over.<br /> <br /> The Devil Tigers of Second Edition worked pretty much the same way. First they make a new Mythos for themselves, and afterwards a Caste based on that Mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about that, really. When I say 'guiderails' I mean in part that they help players deal with the paradox of choice. Part of their value is that they distill a lot of options down to a few. You won't get that same effect with totems unless you have a very small, exhaustive set of totems, which seems like it would hurt totems more than it would help Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T02:02:49-08:00","id":43396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=42934#post42934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ex2 Lunar book was not very impressive art-wise atleast.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e seems to have had problems with its art direction as far as Lunars were concerned.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://fc03.deviantart.net/fs27/f/2008/107/7/c/Abyssals__Recognition_by_kiyo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> On this piece Kiyo said &quot;Yeah, I actually play Exalted, so I do understand the omg shocking horridness. &gt;<img src=\"http://e.deviantart.com/emoticons/letters/=p.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> Made much less horrid by the fact that they wanted her in beastman form and with an expression. Hello, Disney. Oh well.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T03:28:22-08:00","id":43422,"title":"","content":"Manual: Lunars would be a hundred time better if every artworks only have Black Asp's stupid accent and smug-face instead of Wolfguy/Bullguy/Aztecguy. The Storytelling's comic can stay though, because those panels features some very impressive angle (and a non-jail bait Anja is nice too :'D ).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:10:37-08:00","id":43488,"title":"","content":"See I was thinking of this going the other way. The player chooses say 3 keywords (from a fairly decent list) to describe a Totem and then selects whichever animal they want those to be represenative of.<br /> <br /> So Wolf Among the Roses as Totem would be constructed from the keywords: Predator, Seduction, Obfuscation and the player decides that's their version of a Wolf Totem.<br /> <br /> Another player goes with Wolf That Swallows the Sun: Hunger, Darkness, Fear and still uses a Wolf Totem.<br /> <br /> They then get favoured discount on Charms that share one of their selected keywords or maybe different or additional effects for SOME THEMATIC (not all 'cos oh god would that be tough) charms that share one of their keywords.<br /> <br /> Then you could keep Caste as is.<br /> <br /> Or not. I've not even read any of the Lunar books...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:44:47-08:00","id":43510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/42505-thought-exercise-lunar-totems-subsume-and-replace-lunar-castes?p=43488#post43488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I was thinking of this going the other way. The player chooses say 3 keywords (from a fairly decent list) to describe a Totem and then selects whichever animal they want those to be represenative of.<br /> <br /> So Wolf Among the Roses as Totem would be constructed from the keywords: Predator, Seduction, Obfuscation and the player decides that's their version of a Wolf Totem.<br /> <br /> Another player goes with Wolf That Swallows the Sun: Hunger, Darkness, Fear and still uses a Wolf Totem.<br /> <br /> They then get favoured discount on Charms that share one of their selected keywords or maybe different or additional effects for SOME THEMATIC (not all 'cos oh god would that be tough) charms that share one of their keywords.<br /> <br /> Then you could keep Caste as is.<br /> <br /> Or not. I've not even read any of the Lunar books...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. This is pretty much the exact* notion I've had in my head (counts/names are fiddly, of course) ever since John mentioned a system of keywords for Lunar Charms and totems. Honestly, much as I like the idea of shifting Charms around where it's logical and would still like to see that, I find the idea of getting different/additional effects/options on particular, thematic Charms even more interesting.<br /> <br /> I certainly find both more interesting than just setting Caste Attributes; that feels like it just comes down to either having your broad category of totem pre-set, or just picking whatever Attributes you like. It just doesn't feel like it does much to personalize the character. The 9 Attributes are such broad categories: there things in each that may not fit so hot with what you had in mind. I'd much rather something that explicitly takes thematic things and makes them more accessible, potent, or flavorful.<br /> <br /> That said, I am perfectly fine with this kinda thing combined with Attributes set by the totem.<br /> <br /> * Picking Totem/concept first felt important to me, but picking keywords/associations first has a logic I can follow. A minor point, regardless: there's not really a wrong way to build a character.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if the three castes are coming back, they'd probably be much less constraining. Remember, Solars are getting multiple Caste Abilities to choose from for their character. I see absolutely no reason to assume the Lunar Castes <i>wouldn't</i> have multiple Attributes to choose between, regardless of how many Caste/Favored Attributes they get in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}